"""
CivicBridge — Central Government schemes catalogue (browse/discover list).

Important, please read before extending this file:

There is no single official machine-readable master list of all ~700-1,400+
Government of India schemes. The Government's own aggregator, myScheme
(myscheme.gov.in), does not publish a documented public API for its full
catalogue (see scheme_api.py), and independent trackers openly note that no
single authoritative master list exists either.

Given that, this file is a curated, hand-checked catalogue of well-known,
real, currently/recently active Central Sector and Centrally Sponsored
Schemes, grouped by sector and implementing ministry, for USERS TO BROWSE
AND VERIFY — it intentionally does NOT attach fabricated eligibility rules,
invented benefit amounts, or guessed deep-link URLs to each entry. Where a
specific, confidently-known official domain exists it is used; otherwise the
entry points to the relevant ministry/department home page or to the
National Scholarship Portal / myScheme so the person can search for the
current, authoritative page themselves.

This list is large (150+ real schemes) but is NOT exhaustive — it cannot
responsibly be, for the reasons above. For a genuinely complete, always
current catalogue, wire scheme_api.py's SCHEME_API_URL / DATA_GOV_API_KEY
settings to an official data source you have access to (e.g. a data.gov.in
resource ID for Central Government schemes) — sync_api_schemes() will then
pull real records automatically and they will appear in /schemes alongside
this static list.

Every scheme in CivicBridge (this catalogue and benefits_data.py) is
Central Government only — CivicBridge no longer offers a state-scheme mode.
"""

